# Project: map_tests

Procedural world-map preview. Desktop app.

## Tech stack

- **Desktop**: Tauri 2
- **Frontend**: React 19, TypeScript 5.8, Vite 7
- **Backend**: Rust (terrain generation)
- **Package manager**: pnpm
- **Noise**: `noise` (Rust); `simplex-noise` (JS — legacy, do not use for new generation)
- **Parallelism**: `rayon` (Rust)

## Architecture

- Rust is the only source of truth for terrain — the frontend only renders
- Frontend calls Tauri commands via `invoke()` from `src/api/world.ts`
- Canvas rendering: `TerrainGrid` → `ImageData` → `<canvas>`
- Three LOD levels: global → region → chunk
- Seed: `u64` / `number`. Params: `TerrainParams` ↔ `TerrainGenParams`

## Directory layout

```
src/                    # React frontend
  api/world.ts          # Tauri invoke wrappers + types
  hooks/                # useWorldMap, useRegionMap, useChunkMap
  components/Map/       # GlobalMapView, RegionMapView, ChunkMapView
  components/Control/   # SeedControl, BiomeLegend
  map/                  # render.ts, colors.ts
  types/                # world.d.ts, terrainParams.ts
  utils/                # constants.ts
src-tauri/              # Rust backend
  src/world/            # sampler, grid, noise, biome, shape, elevation, ridge, config, prng, types
  src/lib.rs            # Tauri commands
docs/                   # Architecture notes
AGENTS.md               # Agent contract
```

## Domain rules

- **Determinism**: same seed + same params → same world
- **6 shape profiles**: Radial, Ellipse, SquareBump, Irregular, Archipelago, Continents
- Profile comes from `seed % 6` (app default seed: `6` → Ellipse)
- Derived streams (moisture, etc.) from `prng`, not a separate global RNG
- The app runs ONLY as a Tauri desktop app — not as a plain web app
